The metaphysics is getting a little thick here.  Lojban doesn't say much su=
b=20
rosa about what exists or does not; it (like most languages) is just about =
what=20
predicates apply.  No thing comes into existence or passes out of it in {bi=
nxo}=20
and related predicates; rather one set of predicates cease to apply and a n=
ew=20
set come to apply. That is, there is a change of state not of substance. =
=20
Otherwise there would be no change, merely a substitution  (read a good old=
=20
Thomist on the Eucharist).




